I walk over to the register with a big pile of clothes.
The shop assistant smiles at me.
She scans the thick sweater and the green jacket.
She also scans the brown boots, a soft scarf, and a red beanie.
"That will be three thousand five hundred kroner in total," she says.
It is an expensive purchase, but it is very necessary.
I pay with my card.
"Do you want the clothes in a bag?" she asks.
"No thank you," I answer.
"I would like to put the warm clothes on right away."
I take my old, thin sweaters off.
Then I put my new, thick sweater on.
I also put the big green jacket and the soft scarf on.
"You look much warmer now," the shop assistant smiles.
"Yes, thank you very much for the help," I say.
"You are welcome, and have a good day in the cold," she says.
I put my new beanie on and walk out of the shop.
I stand outside on the cold street.
Now I am finally wearing real winter clothes.
I am no longer freezing.
